# R126 (R125's t2): a name that held a kosh is given a raw nirmmita buffer. v300 kept the name marked
# kosh, so a[0] read a kosh length at [a-16] - below the buffer - and the program died with SIGSEGV.
# From v301 a name keeps the kind its first binding gave it: the second assignment is refused.
mukhya() {
    kosh k[4]
    kosh_kship(k, 41)
    vitti a = k
    a = nirmmita(64)
    likh(a, 7)
    likha(a[0])
}
